<title>USA: Phillips Petroleum unit signs Peru deal.</title>
<headline>Phillips Petroleum unit signs Peru deal.</headline>
<dateline>BARTLESVILLE, Okla. 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Phillips Petroleum Co. said on Friday its Phillips Petroleum Peru Ltd subsidiary signed a license contract with Peru's state-owned oil company to explore 3.1 million acres.</p>
<p>Phillips assigned a 50 percent interest in the project ot Agip Exploration BV, a subsidiary of Agip SpA.</p>
<p>The exploration contract signed with Perupetro SA is for seven years. Phillips will be the operator for Block 82, near the  Ucayali Basin along the Brazil border in southeastern Peru.</p>
</text>
